.TH EZBIND 1 "2026-09-21" "ezbind 0.1.0-dev B2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ezbind \- prepare an ebook PDF for folded-folio home bookbinding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ezbind
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.I INPUT.pdf
.B --output
.I OUTPUT.pdf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ezbind
reads one local input PDF and writes a duplex folded-folio arrangement when
folio mode is selected. Each output sheet has two finished-page positions on
each side. The nominal folio assignment is front-left 4, front-right 1,
back-left 2, and back-right 3. Incomplete final folios are padded with blank
logical pages. Cover-only mode instead reads only the supplied front and back
SVG files and writes the separate cover PDF without opening a text-block PDF.
.PP
The current B2 implementation slice supports Letter and A4 sheets, an optional
margin grid, and explicit overwrite control. Physical cover cards, adhesive,
and fabric remain user-supplied.
.PP
The canonical usage statement is:
.PP
.nf
Usage: ezbind [OPTIONS] INPUT.pdf --output OUTPUT.pdf
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help , \-h
Print the usage statement and concise option summary. This operation does not
require an input PDF and returns status 0.
.TP
.B --output \fIPATH\fR, -o \fIPATH\fR
Required output PDF path. The program refuses to replace an existing file
unless \fB--force\fR is specified.
.TP
.BR --sheet\~letter | \-s\~letter | \-\-sheet\~a4 | \-s\~a4
Select the physical output sheet. Letter is the default. Output is landscape:
792 x 612 points for Letter and approximately 841.89 x 595.28 points for A4.
.TP
.BR --grid , \-g
Add light-gray vector grid lines in the margin areas. The current default
spacing is 5 mm. Grid lines are not added unless this option is selected.
.TP
.B --grid-spacing \fIVALUE\fR, -G \fIVALUE\fR
Set the grid spacing. Values require a positive \fBmm\fR, \fBin\fR, or \fBpt\fR value; the default is 5 mm.
.TP
.BR --margin-top\~VALUE | \-t\~VALUE | --margin-bottom\~VALUE | \-b\~VALUE
Set the minimum top or bottom clearance around the uniformly fitted source page. Values require a non-negative \fBmm\fR, \fBin\fR, or \fBpt\fR suffix. The defaults are 36 pt. These are output margins, not source crop values.
.TP
.BR --crop-top\~VALUE | --crop-bottom\~VALUE | --crop-left\~VALUE | --crop-right\~VALUE
Remove the specified source-page edge distances before placement. Values require a non-negative \fBmm\fR, \fBin\fR, or \fBpt\fR suffix and default to zero. Distances are measured from the effective CropBox, falling back to MediaBox, and top/bottom/left/right refer to visual edges after page rotation. Auto-crop is not enabled.
.TP
.BR --margin-fore-edge\~VALUE | \-e\~VALUE | --margin-spine\~VALUE | \-i\~VALUE
Set the minimum fore-edge or spine clearance around the uniformly fitted source page. The spine is the fold-facing inner edge; the fore-edge is outer. Values require a non-negative \fBmm\fR, \fBin\fR, or \fBpt\fR suffix. The defaults are 36 pt and 48 pt.
.TP
.BR --force , \-f
Replace existing folio and cover output PDFs after successful generation. The
program refuses replacement unless this option is specified.
.TP
.B --cover-front \fIPATH\fR
SVG artwork for the front cover. It must be supplied together with the
--cover-back and --cover-output options.
.TP
.B --cover-back \fIPATH\fR
SVG artwork for the back cover. It is rendered on the left half of the
landscape cardstock sheet.
.TP
.B --cover-output \fIPATH\fR
Write a separate one-page cover PDF. The front artwork is rendered on the right
half and the back artwork on the left half, placing both center-cut edges toward
the spine. Artwork is fitted proportionally to each half-sheet viewport. When
cover-only mode is used, no input PDF or folio --output is required; the three
cover options are sufficient and only --cover-output is written.
.SH DEFAULT LAYOUT
The default minimum clearances are 36 points at the top, bottom, and
fore-edge, and 48 points at the spine. The source page is fitted uniformly
inside the resulting content rectangle without distortion. Source crop options
are applied before this fit. If the source and content rectangles have different aspect ratios, additional
letterboxing remains on one pair of edges. The optional grid occupies the
reserved strips and does not cross the source content. A one-page source produces two
physical output sides; source counts are padded to multiples of four.
.SH OUTPUT AND PHYSICAL WORKFLOW
Print the output duplex using the printer setting appropriate for the selected
paper. Fold each sheet once with the fold toward the spine, keep the generated
folio order, and stack before gluing the spine side. Confirm duplex orientation
with a small asymmetric fixture before committing a valuable book.
.PP
When cover mode is selected, print the separate cover PDF on the selected
cardstock size. The back artwork is on the left and the front artwork is on the
right; cut vertically at the center so both cut edges face the spine. Cover
artwork is rendered by librsvg onto a Cairo PDF surface and is fitted
proportionally to each half-sheet viewport.
.PP
Folio and cover output are first written to sibling temporary files and
committed after successful generation. A handled failure does not leave the
temporary output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Input PDF error, including unreadable, malformed, or empty input.
.TP
.B 4
Impossible layout.
.TP
.B 5
Output or filesystem error.
.TP
.B 6
Missing or unusable runtime dependency.
.TP
.B 10
Unexpected internal processing error.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Usage errors are written to standard error and include the diagnostic followed
by the canonical usage line. Ordinary diagnostics do not include extracted
source text, passwords, or complete PDF content.
.SH PDF LIMITATIONS
The qpdf backend preserves visible page content and selectable text for the
implemented folio placement path. Cover artwork is rendered through librsvg
2.58 and Cairo; SVG features outside librsvg's supported static SVG subset,
external resources, and font availability can affect output and must be
validated against representative artwork. Spine/fabric guides,
auto-crop, crop/fold/registration marks, creep, printer safe-area configuration,
and broad document-feature capability reporting are not yet exposed by this B2
slice. Source-page annotations and form fields may not follow clipped content.
Unsupported or degraded backend behavior must be evaluated before production
use.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
ezbind book.pdf -o book-bound.pdf -s a4 -g
.fi
.PP
A separate cardstock cover sheet can be generated with:
.PP
.nf
ezbind book.pdf -o book-bound.pdf --sheet letter \\
  --cover-back back.svg --cover-front front.svg \\
  --cover-output covers.pdf
.fi
.PP
Cover-only generation does not require the text-block PDF:
.PP
.nf
ezbind --sheet letter --cover-back back.svg \\
  --cover-front front.svg --cover-output covers.pdf
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qpdf (1)
